@host = https://localhost:7014

### L01 — First endpoints

### ✅ health → 200 "Healthy"
GET {{host}}/api/health

### ✅ list all orders → 200 with 3 orders
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json

### ✅ get order by id → 200 with one order
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1
Accept: application/json

### ❌ unknown id → 404
GET {{host}}/api/orders/999

### ❌ non-numeric id → 404 (the {id:int} route constraint does not match)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/abc


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L03 — Create order: DTOs, validation, ProblemDetails
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ create order → 201 + Location header, status Pending, server-side prices
# @name createOrder
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Margaret Hamilton",
  "items": [
    { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 2 },
    { "productCode": "mug-01", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### ✅ follow the Location header → 200, same order
GET {{createOrder.response.headers.Location}}

### ✅ fetch it by id from the response body → 200
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### ❌ quantity 1001 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Items[0].Quantity"])
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1001 } ] }

### ❌ empty items → 400 ProblemDetails ("An order needs at least one item.")
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "items": [] }

### ❌ quantity 0 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Items[0].Quantity"])
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 0 } ] }

### ❌ missing customerName → 400, generic "The input was not valid." (no type names)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ❌ blank customerName → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["CustomerName"])
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "   ", "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ❌ unknown product code → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Items[0].ProductCode"])
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "items": [ { "productCode": "TESLA-1", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ❌ overposting: "id" and "status" are ignored → 201 with a NEW id and status "Pending"
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 1, "status": "Paid", "customerName": "Eve", "items": [ { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ❌ malformed JSON → 400, generic message
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada", "items": [


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L04 — Services and DI (no new endpoints: re-run the WHOLE file first; every response must be unchanged)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ create → 201 (singleton keeps it for the next request)
# @name l04Create
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Barbara Liskov", "items": [ { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ✅ a SEPARATE request finds it → 200 (would be 404 if the service were scoped)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{l04Create.response.body.$.id}}

### ❌ null item → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Items[0]"]) — covers the L03 fix bf3ccba
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Ada Lovelace", "items": [ null ] }



### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L05 — Middleware, configuration and options
### Watch the app's console: every request below, including the 404 and the 400s, must log one "HTTP … responded …" line.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ effective settings under Development → 200 { "environment": "Development", "maxItemsPerOrder": 5 }
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/settings
Accept: application/json

### ✅ SAME request under the "https (Production)" profile → 200 { "environment": "Production", "maxItemsPerOrder": 20 }
### (switch the launch profile and re-send: appsettings.Development.json and user secrets are not loaded in Production)
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/settings
Accept: application/json

### ✅ 5 items under Development (the limit) → 201
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Katherine Johnson",
  "items": [
    { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### ❌ 6 items under Development (limit 5) → 400 ProblemDetails, errors["Items"] = "An order can have at most 5 items."
### (under Production the limit is 20, so this same request returns 201)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Katherine Johnson",
  "items": [
    { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### ❌ unknown route → 404, and still logged by the middleware (an action filter would never see it)
GET {{host}}/api/nothing-here

### ❌ Swagger UI under the "https (Production)" profile → 404 (docs exist only in Development)
GET {{host}}/swagger/index.html

    

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L07 — EF Core persistence and migrations
### Re-run the WHOLE file first: every earlier response must be unchanged (orders 1–3 now come from HasData seed rows).
### Rows land in LocalDB database BelsoftEf, tables dbo.Orders and dbo.OrderLines (SQL Server Object Explorer > View Data).
### The L04 note "would be 404 if the service were scoped" no longer applies: the service IS scoped now, and the data survives because it is in SQL Server.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ create order → 201, id generated by SQL Server (IDENTITY)
# @name l07Create
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Edsger Dijkstra", "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 2 }, { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ✅ read it back → 200, total 219.80 (proves Include loaded the lines)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{l07Create.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ✅ PERSISTENCE: stop the app (Shift+F5), start it again (F5), then send this → 200, same order
### Replace 4 with the id returned above if yours differs; a restart clears the named-response variable.
GET {{host}}/api/orders/4
Accept: application/json

### ✅ seed row survives too → 200, Ada Lovelace, total 49.90
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1
Accept: application/json

### ❌ unknown id → 404 (the query ran and found no row)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/999999

### ❌ under the "https (Production)" profile → the app REFUSES TO START:
### "Connection string 'Belsoft' is missing…" (user secrets are Development-only; L29 supplies Production's)
### The L05 Production-profile requests therefore need a connection string from L29 onward.
GET {{host}}/api/orders

### ❌ with a wrong server in user secrets → 500 ProblemDetails, no stack trace, no connection string in the body
### (see the negative check in Step 14; restore the secret afterwards)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L08 — Efficient queries, projections and bounded paging
### GET /api/orders now returns { items, page, pageSize, totalCount, totalPages } of SUMMARIES (no lines).
### The L01 "list all orders" request above returns this envelope from L08 on — a deliberate contract change.
### Watch Output: every list request below must show exactly 2 "Executed DbCommand" lines (COUNT + page),
### the second tagged "-- Orders list page". More than 2 means an N+1 has crept back in.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ default list → 200, page 1, pageSize 20, newest first, each item has lineCount and total
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json

### ✅ filter + sort + paging → 200, only Pending orders whose name contains "a", oldest first, 2 per page
GET {{host}}/api/orders?customer=a&status=Pending&sort=Oldest&page=1&pageSize=2
Accept: application/json

### ✅ page 2 → 200, the NEXT 2 (none repeated from page 1, thanks to the Id tie-breaker)
GET {{host}}/api/orders?customer=a&status=Pending&sort=Oldest&page=2&pageSize=2
Accept: application/json

### ✅ sort by customer → 200, alphabetical
GET {{host}}/api/orders?sort=Customer&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

### ✅ page past the end → 200, items [], totalCount unchanged (not an error: the page simply has nothing)
GET {{host}}/api/orders?page=9999&pageSize=50
Accept: application/json

### ✅ detail endpoint unchanged → 200 with full lines (Include + AsNoTracking)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1
Accept: application/json

### ❌ pageSize=100000 → 200, CLAMPED: "pageSize": 50 in the response, at most 50 items
GET {{host}}/api/orders?pageSize=100000
Accept: application/json

### ❌ page=-1 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Page"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?page=-1

### ❌ page=0 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Page"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?page=0

### ❌ page=10001 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Page"]): caps offset depth and prevents int overflow
GET {{host}}/api/orders?page=10001

### ❌ pageSize=0 → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["PageSize"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?pageSize=0

### ❌ unknown status → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Status"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?status=Teleported

### ❌ unknown sort → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Sort"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?sort=Banana

### ❌ customer longer than 100 characters → 400 ProblemDetails (errors["Customer"])
GET {{host}}/api/orders?customer=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

### ❌ injection attempt in the filter → 200, items [] — the value is a SQL PARAMETER, never part of the SQL text
GET {{host}}/api/orders?customer=%27%3B%20DROP%20TABLE%20Orders%3B--
Accept: application/json


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### L09 — Transactions, state machine and optimistic concurrency
### Re-run the WHOLE file first: earlier responses must be unchanged, except GET /api/orders/{id}, which now also returns an ETag header.
### Send these IN ORDER: each request uses the ETag returned by the one before it.
### Watch Output: each successful transition shows ONE "UPDATE [Orders] … WHERE [Id] = @p… AND [RowVersion] = @p…".
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ create an order to walk through its life → 201, status Pending, ETag header
# @name l09Create
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Hedy Lamarr", "items": [ { "productCode": "MON-27", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### ✅ submit with the current ETag → 200, status Submitted, NEW ETag
# @name l09Submit
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Create.response.body.$.id}}/submit
If-Match: {{l09Create.response.headers.ETag}}

### ✅ pay with the ETag from submit → 200, status Paid, NEW ETag
# @name l09Pay
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Create.response.body.$.id}}/pay
If-Match: {{l09Submit.response.headers.ETag}}

### ✅ ship with the ETag from pay → 200, status Shipped, NEW ETag
# @name l09Ship
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Create.response.body.$.id}}/ship
If-Match: {{l09Pay.response.headers.ETag}}

### ❌ cancel a SHIPPED order (current ETag) → 409 ProblemDetails "The order cannot make that change." / "An order that is Shipped cannot become Cancelled."
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Create.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
If-Match: {{l09Ship.response.headers.ETag}}

### ❌ pay a Pending order (skipping submit) → 409 ProblemDetails "An order that is Pending cannot become Paid."
# @name l09Skip
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Lise Meitner", "items": [ { "productCode": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Skip.response.body.$.id}}/pay
If-Match: {{l09Skip.response.headers.ETag}}

### ── Lost-update race: two updates with the SAME ETag ──

### ✅ create the order both "users" will load → 201
# @name l09Race
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Chien-Shiung Wu", "items": [ { "productCode": "MUG-01", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### ✅ user A submits with the ETag from create → 200, status Submitted
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}/submit
If-Match: {{l09Race.response.headers.ETag}}

### ❌ user B cancels with the SAME (now stale) ETag → 409 "The order was changed by someone else."
### (Cancel from Submitted is LEGAL, so this 409 is purely the version check, not the state machine.)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
If-Match: {{l09Race.response.headers.ETag}}

### ✅ prove nothing was overwritten → 200, status still Submitted (not Cancelled)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ── Header and lookup failures (none of these reach the database) ──

### ❌ no If-Match at all → 428 ProblemDetails "If-Match header required."
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### ❌ malformed If-Match → 400 ProblemDetails "Invalid If-Match header."
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
If-Match: "not-a-version"

### ❌ weak ETag → 400 ProblemDetails (If-Match needs a strong ETag)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{l09Race.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
If-Match: W/"AAAAAAAAB9E="

### ❌ unknown order → 404
POST {{host}}/api/orders/999999/submit
If-Match: "AAAAAAAAB9E="

### ✅ seed order 2 is Paid, so it can be shipped: GET it first and copy its ETag, then send the ship request below
# @name l09Seed2
GET {{host}}/api/orders/2
Accept: application/json

###
POST {{host}}/api/orders/2/ship
If-Match: {{l09Seed2.response.headers.ETag}}